{"id":"00000001794744139763:c4cdee6f9282ad8ab7836531c61cc4e2","text":"2026-11-15 W46 (p265808) main iOS red diagnosis, corrected: RAN the 'Appium/WDA setup' premise is wrong; the 'No simulator found for $RUNTIME_ID' lines are the setup script body echoed, not errors. Two reds: (A) Native iOS Tests (dev, rolldown) hmr-fast-refresh 'a route file created while the app runs becomes reachable' fails on every executed run since Nov 10 (last green dev/rolldown e1ed88f3d7, Nov 8); (B) One Native feature fixtures (iOS) under --bail=1 dies on a varying first test (ShortcutsLink foreground, Warm Shortcuts step, Timeline, Button XCTDaemon launch timeout). RAN locally on current main: rolldown dev server sends the route registry hmr:update ~50ms after app/hmr-added.tsx is created. RAN CI trace run 43694669360: hmr_patch_8 sent 10:40:50.84 and accepted by the app, no bundle refetch after. INFERRED: A is client side, after the registry patch is accepted the app never shows the root welcome-message."}

